  "id": "COMPOUND:42472 - PROTEIN:5805",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between N-Methyltyramine and SCCH-26 through a series of molecular targets. N-Methyltyramine is identified as a target of multiple compounds, including Dehydrogenase/reductase SDR family member 9, Hex-3-en-1-yl 2-methylbut-2-enoate, and Erysimoside. All these compounds are implicated in targeting SCCH-26, a cell line that may be affected by these pathways. The integration of these targets implies a possible mechanism by which N-Methyltyramine interacts with SCCH-26, though the exact nature of this interaction remains unclear. The evidence suggests a potential pathway involving enzymatic activity and cellular response, but further investigation is needed to clarify the specific mechanisms and functional roles of these intermediates.",
